# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (T7), a local named Structure's own code in a callable merge's view: model runs its local S,
# whose code reads the unit's cnt, and returns S\v.  The node w builds runs model's code over its own partial copy of
# the unit, made at the merge, which holds what S's code uses; the root writes cnt after the merge, the copy keeps 7.
# Exit 7.
int: cnt 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        int: v 0
        v: cnt
    S
    return: S\v
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
@: w wrap(5)
cnt: 9
int: result w()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: result; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
